# Key Idea
- Sort both arrays and pair the smallest price with the smallest discount, largest price with largest discount.

# Complexity
- Time complexity: $$O(nlogn)$$

- Space complexity: $$O(1)$$

# Code
```java []
class Solution {
    public double minPrice(int[] prices, int[] discounts) {
        Arrays.sort(prices);
        Arrays.sort(discounts);
        double totalPrice = 0;

        int i = prices.length - 1;
        int j = discounts.length - 1;

        while (i >= 0 && j >= 0) {
            totalPrice += discountedPrice(prices[i], discounts[j]);
            i--;
            j--;
        }

        while (i >= 0) {
            totalPrice += prices[i];
            i--;
        }

        return totalPrice;
    }

    private double discountedPrice(int price, int discount) {
        return (price * (100.0 - discount) / 100.0);
    }
}
```

